// CTO review fixture (OBI-169, PR #72, must-fix 1): a program
// `secure/master.wf`'s `valid_read` denies outright, called into from
// `/std/player` (`triggerleak`). Proves the attribution fix: the error
// raised by `boom()` here must be recorded against `/secure/leak` (the
// program that actually raised it), not `/std/player` (the entry object
// that merely called into it) -- otherwise a `/std` caller could read
// its own, permitted `/std/player` entry and see a message that actually
// originated inside a program it has no `valid_read` access to at all.
pub fn boom() {
    random(0)
}
